{"n": 633, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "633.webp", "text": "tf\n\n33 33071 REPLACING RUBBER\nMOUNTS FOR REAR AXLE\nCARRIER\n\nInstallation\nCheck Installed position of rubber\nmount opening In the rear axle carrier.\n\nRemove rear seat cushion — 52 20 000.\nConvertibles:\n\nRemove side trim panel - 51 43 000.\nSupport trailing arm.\n\nUnscrew strut.\n\nInstallation:\n\nUse washers.\n\nReplace self-locking nuts.\nTihtening torque*.\n\n325 Ix:\nKnock out studs upwards. Rubber mount Is 8 mm (0.315\") higher\nImportant!\n\nDon't damage the threads.\n\nif applicable, cut off protruding rubber\nat the openings.\n\n3033 308\n\nPlace Special Tool 33 3 111 on the\nrubber mount between the body and\nrear axle carrier, and screw In Special\nTool 33 3 101. Heat the rear axle carrier\non the rubber mount take-up to make\nremoval easier.\n\nImportant!\n\nFlat sides of Special Too! 33 3 111 must\nface in direction of the openings. Apply\nSpecial Too! 00 8 550 with its claws in\nthe openings, bolt down with Special\nToo! 33 3 101 and pull out the rubber\nmount.\n\nLonger Special Too! 33 3 107 Is requir-\ned for pulling out in conjunction with\nSpecial Tools 33 3 111 and 00 8 550.\n\nPlace Special Tool on edge of bushing\nbetween the body and rear axle carrier,\nand screw in Special Too! 33 3 103.\nCoat the rubber mount with Circolight**\nand apply on the rear axle carrier, pull-\nIng it In with Special Tool 33 3 104.\n\nNew Special Tool 33 3 115 Is required\nfor pulling In the rubber mount in con-\njunction with Special Tools 33 3 103,\n33 3.112 and 33 3 104,\n\n* See Specifications\n** Source of Supply: HWB", "words": [["tf", 0.0132, 0.6578, 0.0172, 0.6671], ["33", 0.2756, 0.0723, 0.2877, 0.0836], ["33071", 0.2918, 0.0723, 0.3252, 0.0836], ["REPLACING", 0.3338, 0.0723, 0.3992, 0.0836], ["RUBBER", 0.4037, 0.0723, 0.4498, 0.0836], ["MOUNTS", 0.3338, 0.0889, 0.382, 0.1001], ["FOR", 0.386, 0.0889, 0.4088, 0.1001], ["REAR", 0.4134, 0.0889, 0.4438, 0.1001], ["AXLE", 0.4483, 0.0889, 0.47